    "question_raw": "## Level 2 / Searching / Challenge 1\n\n### Problem Description\nThe grandest stage of all, WrestleMania, recently happened. And with it, happened one of the biggest heartbreaks for the WWE fans around the world. \n\nThe Undertaker's undefeated streak was finally over. Now as an Undertaker fan, you're disappointed, disheartened and shattered to pieces.\n\nAnd Randy Orton doesn't want to upset you in any way possible. (After all you are his only friend, true friend!) Randy Orton knows that you're still sensitive to the loss, so he decides to help you out. \n\nEvery time you come across a number, Randy Orton carefully manipulates it. He doesn't want you to face numbers which have \"21\" as a part of them. Or, in the worst case possible, are divisible by 21. \n\nIf you end up facing such a number, you feel sad... and no one wants that - because you start chanting \"The streak is broken!\" , if the number doesn't make you feel sad, you say, \"The streak lives still in our heart!\" Help Randy Orton so that he can help you! \n\n### Constraints\n- 1 \u2264 t \u2264 100 \n- 1 \u2264 n \u2264 1000000 \n\n### Input Format\n- The first line contains a number, `t`, denoting the number of test cases.\n- After that, for `t` lines there is one number in every line. \n\n### Output Format\n- Print the required string, depending on how the number will make you feel.\n\n### Test Cases\n\n#### Test Case 1\n**Input:**\n```\n3\n121\n130\n231\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nThe streak is broken!\nThe streak lives still in our heart!\nThe streak is broken!\n```\n\n#### Test Case 2\n**Input:**\n```\n3\n125\n130\n235\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nThe streak lives still in our heart!\nThe streak lives still in our heart!\nThe streak lives still in our heart!\n```\n\n### Complexity Constraints\n- Cyclomatic Complexity: 7\n- Token Count: 185\n- NLOC: 40\n",
    "has_solution": true,
    "solution_raw": "# Searching - Challenge 1\n\n## 1. Problem Overview\nThe problem requires determining whether a given integer $n$ contains the digit sequence `\"21\"` or is divisible by $21$. If either condition is met, output `\"The streak is broken!\"`; otherwise, output `\"The streak lives still in our heart!\"`.\n\n## 2. Algorithm & Approach\n1. Read the number of test cases $t$.\n2. For each test case, read the number as a string $s$ (and parse its integer value $n$).\n3. Check if $n \\pmod{21} == 0$ or if the substring `\"21\"` exists in $s$ using `strstr(s, \"21\")`.\n4. If either condition holds, print `\"The streak is broken!\"`.\n5. Otherwise, print `\"The streak lives still in our heart!\"`.\n\n## 3. Example Walkthrough\nFor the input:\n- **121**: Contains `\"21\"` as a substring. Output: `The streak is broken!`\n- **130**: $130 \\pmod{21} = 4 \\neq 0$ and does not contain `\"21\"`. Output: `The streak lives still in our heart!`\n- **231**: $231 \\pmod{21} = 0$. Output: `The streak is broken!`\n\n## 4. C Solution\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) != 1) return 0;\n    while (t--) {\n        char s[20];\n        int n;\n        scanf(\"%s\", s);\n        sscanf(s, \"%d\", &n);\n        if (n % 21 == 0 || strstr(s, \"21\") != NULL) {\n            printf(\"The streak is broken!\\n\");\n        } else {\n            printf(\"The streak lives still in our heart!\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n",
    "c_code": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) != 1) return 0;\n    while (t--) {\n        char s[20];\n        int n;\n        scanf(\"%s\", s);\n        sscanf(s, \"%d\", &n);\n        if (n % 21 == 0 || strstr(s, \"21\") != NULL) {\n            printf(\"The streak is broken!\\n\");\n        } else {\n            printf(\"The streak lives still in our heart!\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
