    "question_raw": "## Level 2 / Searching / Challenge 9\n\n### Problem Description\nKanna is upset to learn that no one at his school recognises his initial name. Even his peers refer to him by his surname. Frustrated, he resolves to force his fellow college students to solve this issue in order to get his first name.\n\nKanna has provided each test case a lengthy string containing any ASCII letter as input.\n\nIt's your job to figure out how many times the words SUVO and SUVOJIT appear in it.\n\n### Constraints\n- 0 < T \u2264 100\n- 0 < S \u2264 1000\n\n### Input Format\n- The first line contains the number of testcases, T. \n- Next, T lines follow each containing a long string S.\n\n### Output Format\n- For each long string S, display the no. of times SUVO and SUVOJIT appears in it.\n\n### Test Cases\n\n#### Test Case 1\n**Input:**\n```\n5\nSUVOJITSUVOSUVOJITUCSUVOJITSUVOVXSUVOJITSUVOGMSUVODMMVDSUVOJIT\nAXRSUVOJITHSUVOJITHSUVOJJSUVOJITSUVOJIT\nSUVOJITPRQSUVOJIT\nSUVOJITTXGSUVOUNSUVOJIT\nSUVOJITSUVOSUVOJITXGSUVOSUVOQSUVOJITKDSALASUVOQESUVOHSSUVODFSUVOJITWSUVOUSUVOJITGJEM\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nSUVO = 4, SUVOJIT = 5\nSUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 4\nSUVO = 0, SUVOJIT = 2\nSUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 2\nSUVO = 7, SUVOJIT = 5\n```\n\n#### Test Case 2\n**Input:**\n```\n10\nFSUVOFCOSUVOJITOSUVOAESUVOJITKBSUVOJITSUVOJITSUVOJITFCSUVOJITSUVOSUVOJIT\nSUVOTSUVOSUVOJITGSUVORSUVOSUVOQSUVOJITSUVOTSUVOTXXHYNPSUVO\nSUVOJITSUVO\nSUVOJITSUVORKTSUVOSUVOJITSUVOJITSUVOJITBYGISSUVOJITSUVOSUVOJITRSUVOHSUVO\nSUVOMSUVOSUVO\nWDKLQSUVOJITGSUVOSUVOSUVOJITDSESSUVOJITSUVOYAHY\nMQLSUVOJIT\nSUVOJITOJCSUVOJITVYRHGNLNOWOESUVOJITSUVOJITEYSUVO\nPMSUVOJITMRWJWBSUVOMSUVOXWSUVOJSUVOJIT\nSUVOJITAMSUVOJITONQRVVUQTASUVOJITSUVOJITNBWGQGQSUVORYJRRSUVOJIT\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nSUVO = 3, SUVOJIT = 7\nSUVO = 8, SUVOJIT = 2\nSUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 1\nSUVO = 5, SUVOJIT = 6\nSUVO = 3, SUVOJIT = 0\nSUVO = 3, SUVOJIT = 3\nSUVO = 0, SUVOJIT = 1\nSUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 4\nSUVO = 3, SUVOJIT = 2\nSUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 5\n```\n\n### Mandatory Keywords\n- `0`\n\n### Complexity Constraints\n- Cyclomatic Complexity: 11\n- Token Count: 200\n- NLOC: 36\n",
    "has_solution": true,
    "solution_raw": "# Searching - Challenge 9\n\nAn explanation of the method and the complete C solution are provided below.\n\n## 1. Problem Overview\nThe problem asks us to count the occurrences of the strings `\"SUVO\"` and `\"SUVOJIT\"` within a given set of test case strings. Any occurrence of `\"SUVO\"` that is part of `\"SUVOJIT\"` should be counted exclusively towards `\"SUVOJIT\"` and not towards `\"SUVO\"`.\n\n## 2. Algorithm & Approach\n1. Read the number of test cases $T$.\n2. For each test case, initialize two counters: `suvo = 0` and `suvojit = 0`.\n3. Iterate through each character index $i$ in the string $S$:\n   - Check if the substring starting at index $i$ matches `\"SUVOJIT\"` using `strncmp`. If it matches, increment `suvojit` and advance the pointer by $6$ (so that the loop's `i++` advances past the entire 7-character word).\n   - Otherwise, check if the substring starting at index $i$ matches `\"SUVO\"` using `strncmp`. If it matches, increment `suvo` and advance the pointer by $3$ (advancing past the 4-character word).\n4. Print the result formatted as `SUVO = %d, SUVOJIT = %d`.\n\n## 3. Example Walkthrough\nFor the input:\n`AXRSUVOJITHSUVOJITHSUVOJJSUVOJITSUVOJIT`\n\n- At index 3: matches `\"SUVOJIT\"`, `suvojit` becomes 1. Skip ahead past `\"SUVOJIT\"`.\n- At index 11: matches `\"SUVOJIT\"`, `suvojit` becomes 2. Skip ahead past `\"SUVOJIT\"`.\n- At index 19: matches `\"SUVO\"` followed by `JJ` (not `\"SUVOJIT\"`), `suvo` becomes 1. Skip ahead past `\"SUVO\"`.\n- At index 25: matches `\"SUVOJIT\"`, `suvojit` becomes 3. Skip ahead past `\"SUVOJIT\"`.\n- At index 32: matches `\"SUVOJIT\"`, `suvojit` becomes 4. Skip ahead past `\"SUVOJIT\"`.\n\nFinal output: `SUVO = 1, SUVOJIT = 4`\n\n## 4. C Solution\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) != 1) return 0;\n    while (t--)\n    {\n        char s[1005];\n        scanf(\"%s\", s);\n        int suvo = 0, suvojit = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; s[i] != '\\0'; i++)\n        {\n            if (strncmp(&s[i], \"SUVOJIT\", 7) == 0)\n            {\n                suvojit++;\n                i += 6;\n            }\n            else if (strncmp(&s[i], \"SUVO\", 4) == 0)\n            {\n                suvo++;\n                i += 3;\n            }\n        }\n        printf(\"SUVO = %d, SUVOJIT = %d\\n\", suvo, suvojit);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n",
    "c_code": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) != 1) return 0;\n    while (t--)\n    {\n        char s[1005];\n        scanf(\"%s\", s);\n        int suvo = 0, suvojit = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; s[i] != '\\0'; i++)\n        {\n            if (strncmp(&s[i], \"SUVOJIT\", 7) == 0)\n            {\n                suvojit++;\n                i += 6;\n            }\n            else if (strncmp(&s[i], \"SUVO\", 4) == 0)\n            {\n                suvo++;\n                i += 3;\n            }\n        }\n        printf(\"SUVO = %d, SUVOJIT = %d\\n\", suvo, suvojit);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
