    "question_raw": "## Level 2 / Arrays / Challenge 25\n\n### Problem Description\nAnts have developed advanced ways to find, distribute and make their own food, to such extent that, it has been said that ants eat more meat than lions wolves and tigers combined! \n\nArgentine ant is one of the world\u2019s worst invasive species(Species which are not native to a specific location, but have tendency to spread to a degree to cause damage to the native species of a region) present in the Norfolk Island. \n\nIt forms supercolonies and are aggressive competitors, displacing most other ant species. It can alter ecosystem processes such as pollination and seed dispersal of native plant species.\n\nThe federal environment department is in its mission to wipe out the species from Norfolk Island. So, they are carrying out a survey in T sites within the island examinig the food sources. They know that the ant species can survive in a site only if the food available is more than K units or else they will eventually die out from the site. \n\nFor every site, they go around the region examining N food sources, and finding A[i], the unit of food available from the ith source(1 \u2264 i \u2264 N).\n\nDetermine for each site, whether the ant species can survive or they die out from the specific site.\n\n### Constraints\n- 1 \u2264 T \u2264 100\n- 0 \u2264 K \u2264 1018\n- 1 \u2264 N \u2264 105\n- 0 \u2264 A[i] \u2264 1013\n\n### Input Format\n- The first line contains two space-separated integers T and K. Then, information of T sites of the island follow.\n- For each T, the first line contains N, the number of food sources and the second line contains N space-separated integers, A[i] (1 \u2264 i \u2264 N).\n\n### Output Format\n- For each T, output \"SUCCESS\" without quotes, if the ant species die out or \"FAILURE\" if the ant species survives.\n\n### Test Cases\n\n#### Test Case 1\n**Input:**\n```\n3 8\n2\n4 4\n1\n7\n5\n3 8 11 13 17\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nFAILURE\nSUCCESS\nFAILURE\n```\n\n#### Test Case 2\n**Input:**\n```\n5 7\n2\n5 9\n4\n11 2 7 5\n2\n9 13\n3\n5 7 13\n1\n6\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nFAILURE\nFAILURE\nFAILURE\nFAILURE\nSUCCESS\n```\n\n### Mandatory Keywords\n- `int A[N]`\n- `sum=sum+A[i];`\n\n### Complexity Constraints\n- Cyclomatic Complexity: 6\n- Token Count: 160\n- NLOC: 30\n",
    "has_solution": true,
    "solution_raw": "# Arrays - Challenge 25\n\n## 1. Problem Overview\nThe problem asks us to determine the outcome of an ant eradication mission across $T$ sites. For each site with $N$ food sources and a survival threshold $K$, the ants survive (resulting in `FAILURE` of the eradication mission) if the total available food is at least $K$. Otherwise, if the total food is strictly less than $K$, the ants die out (resulting in `SUCCESS`).\n\n## 2. Algorithm & Approach\n1. Read the number of test cases $T$ and the food requirement $K$.\n2. For each test case:\n   - Read the integer $N$.\n   - Declare the array `int A[N]` to store the food amounts.\n   - Initialize a variable `sum = 0` (using a 64-bit integer to prevent overflow).\n   - Iterate through the $N$ food sources, reading each $A[i]$ and updating `sum=sum+A[i];`.\n   - If `sum >= K`, print `\"FAILURE\"`.\n   - Else, print `\"SUCCESS\"`.\n\n## 3. Example Walkthrough\nFor $T = 3, K = 8$:\n- **Site 1:** $N = 2, A = [4, 4] \\implies \\text{sum} = 8 \\ge 8 \\implies$ Output: `FAILURE`\n- **Site 2:** $N = 1, A = [7] \\implies \\text{sum} = 7 < 8 \\implies$ Output: `SUCCESS`\n- **Site 3:** $N = 5, A = [3, 8, 11, 13, 17] \\implies \\text{sum} = 52 \\ge 8 \\implies$ Output: `FAILURE`\n\n## 4. C Solution\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int T;\n    long long K;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %lld\", &T, &K) != 2) return 0;\n    while (T--)\n    {\n        int N;\n        scanf(\"%d\", &N);\n        int A[N];\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)\n        {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &A[i]);\n            sum=sum+A[i];\n        }\n        if (sum >= K)\n            printf(\"FAILURE\\n\");\n        else\n            printf(\"SUCCESS\\n\");\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n",
    "c_code": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int T;\n    long long K;\n    if (scanf(\"%d %lld\", &T, &K) != 2) return 0;\n    while (T--)\n    {\n        int N;\n        scanf(\"%d\", &N);\n        int A[N];\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)\n        {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &A[i]);\n            sum=sum+A[i];\n        }\n        if (sum >= K)\n            printf(\"FAILURE\\n\");\n        else\n            printf(\"SUCCESS\\n\");\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
