    "question_raw": "## Level 2 / Arrays / Challenge 27\n\n### Problem Description\npathan has a sequence of N integers, A1,A2,...,AN. He likes this sequence if it contains a subsequence of M integers, B1,B2,...,BM within it. A subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from another sequence by deleting some or no elements without changing the order of the remaining elements.\n\nYou will be given a sequence of N integers, A1,A2,...,AN followed by another sequence of M integers, B1,B2,...,BM. Given these, you have to tell whether pathan likes the sequence of N integers(A1,A2,...,AN) or not.\n\nFormally, output \"Yes\" if\n\n\u2203idx1,idx2,...,idxM | 1 \u2264 idx1 < idx2 < ... < idxM \u2264 N and Aidxi = Bi \u2200 i, 1 \u2264 i \u2264 M\n\nOtherwise output \"No\". Note that the quotes are for clarity.\n\n### Constraints\n- 1 \u2264 T \u2264 100\n- 1 \u2264 N \u2264 10^3\n- 1 \u2264 M \u2264 10^3\n- 1 \u2264 Ai, Bi \u2264 10^9\n\n### Input Format\n- The first line contains a single integer, T.\n- T test cases follow where each test case contains four lines:\n- The first line of a test case contains a single integer N\n- The second line of the test case contains N space separated integers, A1,A2,...,AN\n- The third line of the test case contains a single integer M.\n- The fourth line contains M space separated integers, B1,B2,...,BM\n- Symbols have usual meanings as described in the statement.\n\n### Output Format\n- Print the output a single line containing the output. Output is \"Yes\" if Irfan likes the sequence A. \n- Output is \"No\" if pathan dislikes the sequence A.\n\n### Test Cases\n\n#### Test Case 1\n**Input:**\n```\n3\n8\n1 4 3 2 5 6 9 4\n3\n1 7 8\n4\n21 7 16 11\n3\n15 7 3\n4\n1 4 3 2\n3\n1 1 3\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nNo\nNo\nYes\n```\n\n#### Test Case 2\n**Input:**\n```\n3\n6\n3 2 5 6 9 4\n3\n1 7 8\n3\n7 16 11\n3\n15 7 3\n3\n4 3 2\n3\n1 1 3\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nNo\nNo\nNo\n```\n\n### Mandatory Keywords\n- `int no[100],fs[100]`\n\n### Complexity Constraints\n- Cyclomatic Complexity: 10\n- Token Count: 225\n- NLOC: 41\n",
    "has_solution": true,
    "solution_raw": "# Arrays - Challenge 27\n\n## 1. Problem Overview\nThe problem asks us to determine whether a given sequence of $M$ integers ($B$) is a subsequence of another sequence of $N$ integers ($A$). A subsequence is formed by deleting zero or more elements from $A$ without changing the relative order of the remaining elements. We need to print \"Yes\" if $B$ is a subsequence of $A$, and \"No\" otherwise.\n\n## 2. Algorithm & Approach\n1. Read the number of test cases $T$.\n2. For each test case:\n   - Read $N$ and the elements of sequence $A$ into array `no`.\n   - Read $M$ and the elements of sequence $B$ into array `fs`.\n   - Use a two-pointer technique to check if sequence $B$ is a subsequence of $A$:\n     - Initialize two index pointers $i = 0$ (for sequence $A$) and $j = 0$ (for sequence $B$).\n     - Iterate $i$ from $0$ to $N - 1$. Whenever `no[i]` matches `fs[j]`, increment $j$.\n     - Stop early if $j$ reaches $M$.\n   - If $j == M$, output \"Yes\"; otherwise, output \"No\".\n\n## 3. Example Walkthrough\nGiven $N = 8, A = [1, 4, 3, 2, 5, 6, 9, 4]$ and $M = 3, B = [1, 7, 8]$:\n- Step 1: $i = 0 \\implies A[0] = 1, B[0] = 1$. Match found! Advance $j$ to $1$.\n- Step 2: Search for $B[1] = 7$ in remaining elements $[4, 3, 2, 5, 6, 9, 4]$. No match found before reaching end of $A$.\n- End: $j = 1 \\neq M (3)$. Output: `No`.\n\n## 4. C Solution\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t, n, m, i, j;\n    int no[100],fs[100];\n    \n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) == 1) {\n        while (t--) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n            for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                scanf(\"%d\", &no[i]);\n            }\n            scanf(\"%d\", &m);\n            for (i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n                scanf(\"%d\", &fs[i]);\n            }\n            \n            i = 0;\n            j = 0;\n            while (i < n && j < m) {\n                if (no[i] == fs[j]) {\n                    j++;\n                }\n                i++;\n            }\n            \n            if (j == m) {\n                printf(\"Yes\\n\");\n            } else {\n                printf(\"No\\n\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n",
    "c_code": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main()\n{\n    int t, n, m, i, j;\n    int no[100],fs[100];\n    \n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &t) == 1) {\n        while (t--) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n            for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                scanf(\"%d\", &no[i]);\n            }\n            scanf(\"%d\", &m);\n            for (i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n                scanf(\"%d\", &fs[i]);\n            }\n            \n            i = 0;\n            j = 0;\n            while (i < n && j < m) {\n                if (no[i] == fs[j]) {\n                    j++;\n                }\n                i++;\n            }\n            \n            if (j == m) {\n                printf(\"Yes\\n\");\n            } else {\n                printf(\"No\\n\");\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
