    "challenge": "Challenge 38",
    "number": 38,
    "question_raw": "## Level 2 / Linked List / Challenge 38\n\n### Problem Description\nRaguvaran has construct a Apartment. The Apartment is made up of M sections, numbered from 1 to M from left to right. Since he had construct the Apartment in a hurry, not all the sections are of the same height. The i-th section of Apartment is Pi metres tall.\n\nRaguvaran would like to fix his Apartment by reconstructing some of the sections. Raguvaran can set the height of each section he reconstructs to any height he chooses.\n\nRaguvaran will be happy if the number of indices i (1 \u2264 i < M) where Pi \u2260 Pi+1 is not more than K.\n\nWhat is the fewest sections of the Apartment Raguvaran needs to reconstruct so that he will be excitement?\n\n### Constraints\n- 1 \u2264 T \u2264 100.\n- 1 \u2264 Pi \u2264 1000, for all i.\n- 0 \u2264 K \u2264 M.\n- 2 \u2264 M \u2264 100.\n\n### Input Format\n- The first line of the input gives the number of test cases, T. T test cases follow. Each test case begins with a line containing the two integers M and K, the number of sections of Apartment and the maximum number of changes in height between adjacent sections, respectively.\n- The second line contains M integers. The i-th integer is Pi, the height of the i-th section of Apartment.\n\n### Output Format\n- Print the output in a separate lines contains the fewest sections that Raguvaran has to reconstruct so that he will be excitement.\n\n### Test Cases\n\n#### Test Case 1\n**Input:**\n```\n3\n7 3\n300 100 300 300 100 200 500\n5 2\n100 100 100 2\n7 3\n10 20 40 10 10 30 30\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nLine #1: 1\nLine #2: 0\nLine #3: 0\n```\n\n#### Test Case 2\n**Input:**\n```\n2\n8 2\n300 100 300 300 200 100 700 600\n5 2\n100 100 100 100 4\n```\n**Expected Output:**\n```\nLine #1: 3\nLine #2: 0\n```\n\n### Mandatory Keywords\n- `for`\n\n### Complexity Constraints\n- Cyclomatic Complexity: 1\n- Token Count: 720\n- NLOC: 81\n",
    "has_solution": true,
    "solution_raw": "# Linked List - Challenge 38\n\n## 1. Problem Overview\nThe problem asks for the minimum number of sections (elements) in an array $P$ of length $M$ that need to be modified (reconstructed) such that the number of height transitions between adjacent sections ($P_i \\neq P_{i+1}$) is at most $K$.\n\n## 2. Algorithm & Approach\n1. **Reformulation**: Minimizing the number of modified sections is equivalent to maximizing the number of original sections kept unchanged. Allowing at most $K$ height changes means partitioning the array into at most $K + 1$ contiguous subsegments, where each subsegment is assigned a single height.\n2. **Subsegment Cost**: For any subsegment $P[p..i-1]$, the maximum number of unchanged elements we can keep is the maximum frequency of any element value present in that subsegment.\n3. **Dynamic Programming**:\n   - Define `dp[i][j]` as the maximum number of elements kept unchanged in prefix $P[0..i-1]$ using at most $j$ subsegments (which corresponds to $j-1$ height transitions).\n   - Base Case: `dp[0][j] = 0` for all $j$.\n   - Transition: For each prefix $i$ and subsegment count $j$:\n     $$\\text{dp}[i][j] = \\max_{0 \\le p < i} \\left( \\text{dp}[p][j-1] + \\text{max\\_freq}(P[p..i-1]) \\right)$$\n4. The answer for a test case is $M - \\text{dp}[M][\\min(K+1, M)]$.\n\n## 3. Example Walkthrough\nConsider Test Case 2, Case 1: $M = 8, K = 2$, Array = `[300, 100, 300, 300, 200, 100, 700, 600]`\n- $K = 2 \\implies$ At most $3$ segments allowed.\n- Segment 1: `[300, 100, 300, 300]` $\\rightarrow$ Most frequent element is `300` (appears 3 times).\n- Segment 2: `[200, 100]` $\\rightarrow$ Most frequent element appears 1 time.\n- Segment 3: `[700, 600]` $\\rightarrow$ Most frequent element appears 1 time.\n- Total maximum unchanged elements = $3 + 1 + 1 = 5$.\n- Minimum sections to reconstruct = $M - 5 = 8 - 5 = 3$.\n- Output: `Line #1: 3`.\n\n## 4. C Solution\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int T, t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &T) != 1) return 0;\n    for (t = 1; t <= T; t++) {\n        int M, K, i, j, p;\n        if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &M, &K) != 2) break;\n        int a[105];\n        for (i = 0; i < M; i++) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n        }\n\n        int dp[105][105] = {0};\n        int max_blocks = K + 1 > M ? M : K + 1;\n\n        for (j = 1; j <= max_blocks; j++) {\n            for (i = 1; i <= M; i++) {\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 1];\n                int counts[1005] = {0};\n                int max_f = 0;\n                for (p = i - 1; p >= 0; p--) {\n                    counts[a[p]]++;\n                    if (counts[a[p]] > max_f) {\n                        max_f = counts[a[p]];\n                    }\n                    if (dp[p][j - 1] + max_f > dp[i][j]) {\n                        dp[i][j] = dp[p][j - 1] + max_f;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int max_kept = dp[M][max_blocks];\n        printf(\"Line #%d: %d\\n\", t, M - max_kept);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n",
    "c_code": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int T, t;\n    if (scanf(\"%d\", &T) != 1) return 0;\n    for (t = 1; t <= T; t++) {\n        int M, K, i, j, p;\n        if (scanf(\"%d %d\", &M, &K) != 2) break;\n        int a[105];\n        for (i = 0; i < M; i++) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n        }\n\n        int dp[105][105] = {0};\n        int max_blocks = K + 1 > M ? M : K + 1;\n\n        for (j = 1; j <= max_blocks; j++) {\n            for (i = 1; i <= M; i++) {\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 1];\n                int counts[1005] = {0};\n                int max_f = 0;\n                for (p = i - 1; p >= 0; p--) {\n                    counts[a[p]]++;\n                    if (counts[a[p]] > max_f) {\n                        max_f = counts[a[p]];\n                    }\n                    if (dp[p][j - 1] + max_f > dp[i][j]) {\n                        dp[i][j] = dp[p][j - 1] + max_f;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        int max_kept = dp[M][max_blocks];\n        printf(\"Line #%d: %d\\n\", t, M - max_kept);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}"
